# ESP32 Gas Detection and Automatic Fan Control

## About
This project uses an ESP32 with MQ2 and MQ135 gas sensors
to monitor gas levels and automatically control a PWM fan.

## Features
- Monitors MQ2 and MQ135 sensors
- Automatically increases fan speed when gas levels are high
- Sends sensor readings to Raspberry Pi using UART
- Data is transmitted every 3 seconds

## Hardware
- ESP32
- MQ2 Gas Sensor
- MQ135 Gas Sensor
- PWM Fan
- Raspberry Pi

## Pin Connections
- MQ2 → GPIO34
- MQ135 → GPIO35
- Fan → GPIO21
- ESP32 TX2 → GPIO17

## Communication
Baud Rate: 115200

Example:
MQ2:875
MQ135:640
